[3] iteration in the *UV* (inverse-blocking) direction, wall -> crossover
    k* = (beta_c - beta_wall) / (C_N ln b) ;  scale factor 2^k*
    N       beta_wall     beta_c       k*       2^k*
    2         0.08333      2.500    9.385      668.5
    3         0.18750      5.690    9.497      722.5
    => ~9.4-9.5 steps for BOTH N: k* = (beta_c-beta_wall)/(C_N ln b) is N-independent
       because beta_c ~ N^2 and C_N ~ N^2 cancel.  Ceiling: 10 steps.
    BUT this direction is *adding* degrees of freedom (mu increases): it is not
    the pushforward of a measure, it needs a UV completion.  No theorem; no map.

[4] why a power law cannot help at d=4 (engineering dimension)
    beta_W = 2N/(g^2 a^(4-d)) ; at fixed g, a -> b a gives beta_eff = b^(4-d) beta
      d=2 : exponent 4-d = +2  ->  beta_eff/beta = b^+2 = 4.0000 (b=2)
      d=3 : exponent 4-d = +1  ->  beta_eff/beta = b^+1 = 2.0000 (b=2)
      d=4 : exponent 4-d = +0  ->  beta_eff/beta = b^+0 = 1.0000 (b=2)
    d=4 is exactly marginal: exponent 0, so the leading term is beta_eff = beta.
    The whole flow is logarithmic and its SIGN is the one-loop coefficient (AF).
    d<4 is the opposite case: exponent 4-d>0, beta grows, IR weak coupling
    (super-renormalisable) -- which is why only d=4 has the hard end at the IR.
    d=2 'beta_eff = b^2 beta' is thus a dimensional artifact of the normalisation,
    not a flow statement: in 2D the physical gap m = C2 g^2/2 does not move.

[5] cross-check against the stored activity-matched step (T1-POLYMER-RG §4, §6)
    activity-matched:  u(2.5)=1.014 -> u_eff=0.988  =>  beta_eff^act=2.40, ratio=0.960
    coupling one-loop:                             beta_eff    =2.242, ratio=0.897
    two independent definitions of the same step -> both <1 (0.96 / 0.90).
    sign is scheme-independent; the SIZE is scheme-dependent. No scheme gives >1.

[6] four-model test of a block-spin-type quantity (Q_BS := one-step beta flow)
    free field         0          beta=inf, g=0 exactly: no flow, Q_BS=0                     [T]
    2D YM              >0         exact Migdal blocking, Q_BS!=0 and m=C2 g^2/2>0            [T]
    M6                 NOT 0      Gaussian marginal is an exact RG fixed point: the a-marginal of M6 [T]
    M6 (cont.)                    equals that of the gapped HO (sup|drho|=2.3e-14, U09 §3)   
    single plaquette   undefined  no thermodynamic limit, no tower                           [T]
    => two horns, both fatal: (i) if Q_BS sees only the blocked (a) marginal, then
       Q_BS(M6) = Q_BS(HO) exactly (2.3e-14) => it cannot read 0 on M6 and >0 on HO;
       (ii) if it sees the free (b) direction, it must be min-type => it is the gap
       itself (U05) => circular.  4-model: FAIL on both horns.

[7] verdict
    (a) beta_eff > beta  with a theorem : NO  -> (a) not triggered
    (b) fixed-b block-spin theorems exist for phi^4_4 (GK) and 4D U(1) (Gopfert-Mack,
        strong-coupling/dipole route); for SU(N) at fixed b: none  -> (b) triggered
    (c) beta_eff < beta : YES, one loop exactly, ratio 0.90 (N=2) at the crossover;
        the only beta-raising direction is inverse blocking (UV), 10 steps, no map
        -> (c) TRIGGERED: the flow points away from 2.5.

